  "system": {
    "identifier": "senju-wood-release-great-forest-technique",
    "description": "<p>You change the structure of your arms or legs into that of Chakra enhanced wood. You transform your appendage into a fork of multiple branches.</p>\n<p>Make a melee Ninjutsu attack against a creature you can see within range. On a hit you deal 4d8 Earth, Cold or Chakra damage and the target must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, they are grappled by you.</p>\n<p>A creature grappled by you can be pulled 10 feet closer towards you as a bonus action on each of your turns. A grappled creature can spend its action to remake its saving throw to escape this grapple on a success.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3, damage by 1d8 and range by 5 feet.</p>",
